### What was already delivered (prior loop commit `d722374e`)
Generic, registry-backed TTS path with no `kokoro`/`inworld` branches on the dispatch surface:

| Surface | Change |
|---|---|
| **`studio/tts/dispatch.py`** | Single path for provider resolve, voice pick (P5), settings merge, cache, synthesize, reconciled `metadata`/`job_meta` |
| **`studio/pipeline/services.py`** | `_step_tts` → `dispatch.synthesize` (branches removed) |
| **`studio/tts/routes.py`** | generate / voices / stream use registry + capabilities |
| **`studio/workflows/adapters/tts.py`** | Provider-agnostic via `provider_id` + dispatch |
| **`studio/workflows/options.py`** | `tts_voices` → `dispatch.list_voices` (per selected provider) |
| **Frontend** | `ConfigField` sends `options_context` (`domain`, `provider`) so the voice dropdown follows the node’s provider |

### Done criteria
- Legacy TTS API + unchanged `tts.generate` produce compatible artifacts for both providers  
- Saved `engine` configs migrate and run (`test_a_saved_engine_configuration_migrates_and_then_runs`)  
- Voice dropdown: Kokoro vs Inworld (and live Inworld list via `list_voices`)  
- One reconciled metadata/`job_meta` shape  
- Fixture TTS provider runs zero-touch through the node  
- Mocked + local Kokoro tests green  

